rac{4 - 4i \\pm \\sqrt{(4 - 4i)^2 + 4i}}{2}\n   \\]\n   Simplify the discriminant:\n   \\[\n   (4 - 4i)^2 + 4i = 16 - 32i + 16i^2 + 4i = 16 - 32i - 16 + 4i = -28i\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   z = \\frac{4 - 4i \\pm \\sqrt{-28i}}{2} = \\frac{4 - 4i \\pm 2\\sqrt{7}i}{2} = 2 - 2i \\pm \\sqrt{7}i\n   \\]\n   So the roots are:\n   \\[\n   z_1 = 2 - 2i + \\sqrt{7}i, \\quad z_2 = 2 - 2i - \\sqrt{7}i\n   \\]\n\n   Solve \\(z^2 + 4iz - i = 0\\) using the quadratic formula:\n   \\[\n   z = \\frac{-4i \\pm \\sqrt{(4i)^2 + 4i}}{2} = \\frac{-4i \\pm \\sqrt{-16 + 4i}}{2} = \\frac{-4i \\pm 2\\sqrt{1 + i}}{2} = -2i \\pm \\sqrt{1 + i}\n   \\]\n   So the roots are:\n   \\[\n   z_3 = -2i + \\sqrt{1 + i}, \\quad z_4 = -2i - \\sqrt{1 + i}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Vertices of the polygon:**\n   The roots are:\n   \\[\n   z_1 = 2 - 2i + \\sqrt{7}i, \\quad z_2 = 2 - 2i - \\sqrt{7}i, \\quad z_3 = -2i + \\sqrt{1 + i}, \\quad z_4 = -2i - \\sqrt{1 + i}\n   \\]\n\n7. **Calculate the area of the polygon:**\n   The area of the polygon formed by these vertices can be found using the Shoelace formula or by recognizing the symmetry and geometric properties of the roots. Given the symmetry and the form of the roots, the area simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Area} = 2^2 = 4\n   \\]\n\nThus, the area of the polygon is \\(4\\), which can be expressed as \\(4 = 2^2\\). Therefore, \\(a = 2\\), \\(b = 2\\), and \\(p = 2\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
